    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86605834960938,
        102.29456329345703,
        527.3919067382812,
        116.73756408691406
      ],
      "text": "The treatment completion rate in the levofloxacin arm was 86% in TB CHAMP (placebo arm: 86%)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86605834960938,
        115.49457550048828,
        527.3953857421875,
        129.9375762939453
      ],
      "text": "and 70% in V-QUIN (placebo arm: 85%), with RRs of 1.00 [95% CI 0.95 ; 1.06] and 0.83 [0.79 ; 0.87],",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86605834960938,
        128.69459533691406,
        527.3865356445312,
        143.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "respectively. There was an important difference in the risk of adverse events between children and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86605834960938,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.4243774414062,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "adults, with very good tolerance in children, which decreased with age. This probably contributed to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.3788452148438,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "poorer adherence to TPT by the participants in the V-QUIN. The prevalence of adverse events of grade",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.953652381896973,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.29469299316406,
        527.1222534179688,
        182.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "3 or more was not significantly higher in the TB CHAMP trial among people < 18 years receiving 6Lfx",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.995949745178223,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.4947052001953,
        527.398193359375,
        195.9376983642578
      ],
      "text": "(RR 0.53, 95% CI 0.16 ; 1.70), but significantly higher rates were found in the V-QUIN trial, in which",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69471740722656,
        527.5040893554688,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "97% of participants were > 14 years (RR 5.26, 95% CI 1.16 ; 23.95). Overall, the likelihood of treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97892951965332,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.414794921875,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "discontinuation among individuals on 6LFx with adverse events of any grade was high (RR 6.32, 95%",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.09474182128906,
        527.3958129882812,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "CI 3.43 ; 11.63), occurring in 43 more patients out of 1000 (range, 20–89). Microbiological studies",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        234.29469299316406,
        527.081787109375,
        248.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "within both trials did not provide conclusive evidence of the emergence of additional fluoroquinolone",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.982436180114746,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        246.2187042236328,
        524.4157104492188,
        261.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis  resistance in TB strains or in microbiota other than  (e.g. gut flora) at the time of analysis.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.958572387695312,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        269.1986083984375,
        527.2501220703125,
        283.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "A systematic review of studies published between June 2016 and September 2023 identified five",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        282.39862060546875,
        527.4168090820312,
        296.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "observational studies of adverse events with fluoroquinolone (alone or in combination with other TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        295.5986328125,
        527.4784545898438,
        310.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "drugs). All were observational studies with substantial risk of bias, notably selection and ascertainment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.972765922546387,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        308.798583984375,
        527.1595458984375,
        323.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "bias. Fluoroquinolone monotherapy with levofloxacin, ofloxacin or moxifloxacin was found to be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.99859619140625,
        527.41015625,
        336.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "generally safe in three studies, with some mild or moderate drug-related adverse events in children",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        335.1986083984375,
        440.905029296875,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "but no grade 3 or 4 or serious adverse events reported. (For more details, see",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        441.5929870605469,
        335.1986083984375,
        488.2198181152344,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "annexes 4",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        488.2210998535156,
        335.1986083984375,
        512.4595947265625,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        513.194580078125,
        335.1986083984375,
        518.8595581054688,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "5",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        518.861083984375,
        335.1986083984375,
        527.4190673828125,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": ".)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86602783203125,
        348.39862060546875,
        527.4464111328125,
        362.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "No evidence was found to support shortening of levofloxacin TPT to < 6 months or its prolongation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86602783203125,
        361.5986022949219,
        154.43649291992188,
        376.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "months. beyond 6",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.37223052978516,
        386.4652099609375,
        230.94537353515625,
        404.7352294921875
      ],
      "text": "Subgroup considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        411.33111572265625,
        527.481689453125,
        425.8841247558594
      ],
      "text": "Children and adolescents : Levofloxacin can be used in children and adolescents, in whom completion",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 10.945363998413086,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        424.64111328125,
        527.3876953125,
        439.0841369628906
      ],
      "text": "and tolerability in the TB CHAMP trial (which included only individuals aged < 18 years) were much",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        437.8412170410156,
        527.4188842773438,
        452.28424072265625
      ],
      "text": "better than in the V-QUIN trial (in which 97% of participants were aged ≥ 15 years). There is no",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        451.0411071777344,
        527.4598388671875,
        465.484130859375
      ],
      "text": "requirement to test for TBI before starting levofloxacin in children who are contacts of people with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        464.2411193847656,
        527.4432373046875,
        478.68414306640625
      ],
      "text": "MDR/RR-TB. Although there has been concern about use of fluoroquinolones in children because of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        476.16510009765625,
        527.4057006835938,
        491.8841247558594
      ],
      "text": "(119) retardation of cartilage development shown in juvenile animals exposed to these agents  , similar",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.994098663330078,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        489.3651123046875,
        294.2104797363281,
        505.0841369628906
      ],
      "text": "(120,121) effects have not been found in humans  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        512.235107421875,
        527.5010986328125,
        526.7880859375
      ],
      "text": "Pregnancy and breastfeeding : TPT with levofloxacin in pregnancy requires a risk–benefit assessment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 10.964643478393555,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        525.5451049804688,
        527.4376831054688,
        539.9880981445312
      ],
      "text": "and an informed choice by pregnant woman on whether to take TPT or to defer TPT to the end of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        538.7451171875,
        527.4180297851562,
        553.1881103515625
      ],
      "text": "pregnancy. The advice should depend on the circumstances (e.g. first trimester versus later). Pregnancy",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.95269775390625,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        551.945068359375,
        527.4383544921875,
        566.3880615234375
      ],
      "text": "increases the risk of progression from infection to disease and the risk of poor maternal and fetal",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        565.1451416015625,
        527.3892211914062,
        579.588134765625
      ],
      "text": "outcomes should TB disease occur. MDR/RR-TB in pregnancy is a serious condition, and some of the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        578.3450927734375,
        527.5751953125,
        592.7880859375
      ],
      "text": "drugs used to treat MDR-TB may be toxic to the fetus. Observations from studies in animals exposed",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.997149467468262,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        591.5451049804688,
        527.5846557617188,
        605.9880981445312
      ],
      "text": "to levofloxacin have limited its use in pregnancy; however, one meta-analysis of observational studies",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.990095138549805,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        604.7451171875,
        527.408203125,
        619.1881103515625
      ],
      "text": "with 2800 pregnant women given fluoroquinolones for any indication (e.g. urinary tract infection)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        617.945068359375,
        527.279541015625,
        632.3880615234375
      ],
      "text": "found no difference in the incidence of birth defects, spontaneous abortion or prematurity from",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        629.869140625,
        527.4019775390625,
        645.588134765625
      ],
      "text": "(122) that in unexposed pregnant women  . The concentrations of levofloxacin in breastmilk appeared",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        644.3450927734375,
        527.38818359375,
        658.7880859375
      ],
      "text": "to be far lower than the dose for infants and would not be expected to cause adverse effects in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        656.2691040039062,
        527.5048828125,
        671.9880981445312
      ],
      "text": "(123) breastfed infants . Its use should therefore not be suspended during breastfeeding. While effects",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.990495681762695,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        670.7451171875,
        527.3397216796875,
        685.1881103515625
      ],
      "text": "of fluoroquinolones on bone and cartilage observed in animals have not been seen in humans,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        683.945068359375,
        527.43994140625,
        698.3880615234375
      ],
      "text": "the data and follow-up times of infants are limited. Recent alerts have, however, highlighted safety",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        695.869140625,
        444.9394836425781,
        711.588134765625
      ],
      "text": "(124–126) concerns associated with prolonged use of fluoroquinolones in humans  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        718.739013671875,
        527.39208984375,
        733.2919921875
      ],
      "text": "HIV infection : Levofloxacin can be used in people with HIV. No specific drug–drug interaction with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        732.0490112304688,
        527.3751831054688,
        746.4920043945312
      ],
      "text": "ART has been observed in people with HIV exposed to MDR/RR-TB, and there is no need to test for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        745.2490234375,
        239.0908203125,
        759.6920166015625
      ],
      "text": "infection before starting levofloxacin.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
